ch30 < A room full of sleepers has a shape, and he had known this one's for five nights. Brom made the most of it, in the middle, breathing like something felled. Lira lay on her right side, a yard from Cael's elbow, and Karis by the boxes, small and quick, with a catch at the top of every breath that had been there since a cook-house. There was the old man's, upright, by the gable. And there was a place near the ladder's head where nothing was. He had learned to know it as a person knows where a rug lies in a dark room, because the floor does not ring there.
